@startuml UC-SPRINT-CANCEL
' UC-22 - Cancel Sprint | semantic key: UC-SPRINT-CANCEL
' Source: data/use_cases/sprint-management/UC-SPRINT-CANCEL.yml
' Business Rules: BR-SPRINT-CANCEL-PO-ONLY, BR-SPRINT-INCOMPLETE-RETURN-BACKLOG
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' One Activity Final shared by all paths (team decision 2026-10-05; UML allows one or several). It
' is reached after the Sprint is cancelled, items returned and reason and timestamp recorded
' (postconditions met) or with the Sprint unchanged (EX-01 rejection, AF-01 continuation).
' AF-01.1 (the Product Owner cancels the confirmation) is the [continue Sprint — AF-01] outcome
' of the Product Owner's confirmation decision.
' EX-01 occurs "before the cancellation is confirmed", so the System checks the Sprint state
' after the confirmation (NF3) and before cancelling (NF4).
' Layout (2026-10-06): the decision "Confirm cancellation?" is drawn in the System lane, where the
' System waits for the Product Owner's answer; the guards name the Product Owner's choice. In the
' Product Owner lane its merge forced a detour across the lanes. The final stays in the System lane.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|PRO| $lane_title("Product Owner")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|PRO|
start
' [NF1, BR-SPRINT-CANCEL-PO-ONLY]
:Request Sprint cancellation
and provide reason;
|SYS|
' [NF2]
:Display impact on selected
and completed work;
if ($question("Confirm cancellation?")) then ($guard_left("[confirm]"))
  |PRO|
  ' [NF3]
  :Confirm cancellation;
  |SYS|
  if ($question_x("Sprint still active?")) then ($guard_left("[active]"))
    ' [NF4, POST1]
    :Cancel active Sprint;
    ' [NF4, POST2, BR-SPRINT-INCOMPLETE-RETURN-BACKLOG]
    :Return incomplete items
    to Product Backlog;
    ' [NF5]
    :Record cancellation
    reason and timestamp;
  else ($guard_right("[completed or", "cancelled — EX-01]"))
    ' [EX-01, GUIDE-7.3]
    :Reject Sprint cancellation;
  endif
else ($guard_right("[continue", "Sprint — AF-01]"))
  |SYS|
  ' [AF-01.2]
  :Leave Sprint unchanged;
endif
|SYS|
stop
@enduml
